 We want to show that there is an index 
\begin_inset Formula $u:Z\rightarrow\mathbb{R}$
\end_inset

 such that 
\begin_inset Formula $\succsim$
\end_inset

 is represented by the function 
\begin_inset Formula $U:\Delta(Z)\rightarrow\mathbb{R}$
\end_inset

 defined by: 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\ \pi\in\Delta(Z):U(\pi)\equiv E_{\pi}u$
\end_inset

.
 By Proposition 58, there are lotteries 
\begin_inset Formula $\{\overline{\pi},\underline{\pi}\}\subseteq\Delta(Z)$
\end_inset

 such that for each 
\begin_inset Formula $\pi\in\Delta(Z)$
\end_inset

,
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\overline{\pi}\succsim\pi\succsim\underline{\pi}
\]

\end_inset

We can suppose without loss of generality that 
\begin_inset Formula $\overline{\pi}\succ\underline{\pi}$
\end_inset

, for otherwise the theorem is trivial.
 We will proceed in five steps.
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Enumerate
