\begin_layout Proof
First, we analyze the 
\begin_inset Formula $EU$
\end_inset

 associated with 
\begin_inset Formula $u$
\end_inset

.
 In this case, the indifference sets are linear and parallel.
 Set 
\begin_inset Formula $ $
\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $EU=3$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\pi(z_{2})=0$
\end_inset

.
 Then, 
\begin_inset Formula $\pi(z_{1})+\pi(z_{3})=1$
\end_inset

, and
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{gather*}
EU=\pi(z_{1})+100\pi(z_{3})=3\\
=1-\pi(z_{3})+100\pi(z_{3})=3\\
\pi(z_{3})=\frac{2}{99}\\
\pi(z_{1})=\frac{97}{99}
\end{gather*}

\end_inset


\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset

Next, we analyze the 
\begin_inset Formula $EU$
\end_inset

 associated with 
\begin_inset Formula $100u$
\end_inset

.
 In this case, the indifference sets are once again linear and parallel.
 Set 
\begin_inset Formula $EU=300$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\pi(z_{2})=0$
\end_inset

.
 Then, 
\begin_inset Formula $\pi(z_{1})+\pi(z_{3})=1$
\end_inset

, and
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{gather*}
EU=100\pi(z_{1})+10,000\pi(z_{3})=300\\
=100(1-\pi(z_{3}))+10,000\pi(z_{3})=300\\
\pi(z_{3})=\frac{2}{99}\\
\pi(z_{1})=\frac{97}{99}
\end{gather*}

\end_inset

Therefore, the 
\begin_inset Formula $EU$
\end_inset

 associated with 
\begin_inset Formula $100u$
\end_inset

 represents the same preference as the original 
\begin_inset Formula $EU$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Proof
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset

Finally, we analyze the 
\begin_inset Formula $EU$
\end_inset

 associated with 
\begin_inset Formula $u^{2}$
\end_inset

.
 Set 
\begin_inset Formula $EU=9$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\pi(z_{2})=0$
\end_inset

.
 Then, 
\begin_inset Formula $\pi(z_{1})+\pi(z_{3})=1$
\end_inset

, and
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{gather*}
EU=\pi(z_{1})+10,000\pi(z_{3})=9\\
=(1-\pi(z_{3}))+10,000\pi(z_{3})=9\\
\pi(z_{3})=\frac{8}{9999}\\
\pi(z_{1})=\frac{991}{9999}
\end{gather*}

\end_inset

Therefore, the 
\begin_inset Formula $EU$
\end_inset

 associated with 
\begin_inset Formula $u^{2}$
\end_inset

 does not represent the same preference as the original 
\begin_inset Formula $EU$
\end_inset

.
 In addition, the indifference sets are no longer linear and parallel.
